diff --git a/docs/architecture/j2k-reset.md b/docs/architecture/j2k-reset.md
index 9d7e20fc3f5a25145eed64881336758d18afbdf8..6d94e35a82df51e7ac1e648dcdff5cfb1cc0c57c 100644
--- a/docs/architecture/j2k-reset.md
+++ b/docs/architecture/j2k-reset.md
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ Novel integration uses a small set of presentation adapters rather than parallel
 
 The novel reader inflates J2K's existing `reader_activity` and binds its existing app bar, toolbar, viewer container, navigation controls, chapter sheet, and slider. Hayai applies system-bar and display-cutout insets at that shared layout boundary. While reader chrome is visible, the novel viewer starts after the system inset and toolbar height; when chrome visibility changes, the same inset binding recalculates the viewer margin. This avoids a second novel-specific safe-area model and keeps the image-reader activity unchanged.
 
